From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:24:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] chatlist: hide contact requests behind a requests link

Someone who is already in a group with you can keep creating lookalike
copies of it and adding you. Each copy is a new contact request chat, so
each one takes a row at the top of the chat list (and, being newly
created, raises a notification), burying the real conversations.

Add a DC_GCL_NO_REQUESTS chatlist flag. With it the normal chatlist
leaves contact requests (blocked=2) out and, unless DC_GCL_NO_SPECIALS is
set, puts the new DC_CHAT_ID_REQUESTS_LINK (8) pseudo chat on top when
any unarchived request exists, mirroring DC_CHAT_ID_ARCHIVED_LINK; the
"all done" hint is not added while requests wait. Archived requests stay
in the archive like any archived chat and are not counted.

The requests themselves are listed with a new `is:request` query
keyword, handled like `is:unread` and composable with search text. With
DC_GCL_NO_REQUESTS, a query made only of filter keywords (e.g. a bare
`is:unread`) also leaves requests out; typed search text still finds
them.

JSON-RPC returns the link as ChatListItemFetchResult::RequestsLink, whose
fresh_message_counter is the number of requests (get_request_cnt). That
count only changes when the set of chats changes, so
emit_chatlist_changed also emits ChatlistItemChanged for the link, and
accepting a request now emits ChatlistChanged (it moves the chat from
the requests link into the normal list).
